Z||000000||LAMBO||09-13-2000||03:23 PM||||Has anyone bought and installed the Gorlic exhaust system from the Fiero Store. If so, what are your impressions. I'm needing to replace exhaust from the cat. on back.<BR>Thanks, Todd ||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||09-13-2000||09:15 PM||||I have one on one of my Fiero's. Works fine, sounds normal and is generally good. I prefer a quiet exhaust. It sounds good outside and is nice inside.<P>I did find that the bends were a bit off in position, so I took it down to a muffler shop and for $30, they heated and repositioned the outlet pipes/tips.<P>Year old and still sealed. Backpressure is actually pretty low at 1.5PSI on snap and wot.<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000002||LAMBO||09-14-2000||09:42 AM||||Thanks Terrk. Exactly what I wanted to know. I'm putting this on my everyday driver and I want something fairly quiet.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Linx||09-14-2000||06:33 PM||||Lambo-  my recommendation is to take it to Midas.  We tend to forget that not everything on our fiero's is hard to come by.  And its a good sounding muffler, lifetime warrenty and they get to put it in for you.  It's cheaper, too- $160 and they bust their knuckles.||||reg||1
Z||000004||LAMBO||09-15-2000||03:56 PM||||Hi Linx, woulda done it if it wasn't for the motor and cradle sitting out in the middle of my garage floor. I'm in the midst of an engine swap. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
